# rm213, the quiet hinge (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm213
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rm_theodora_wickley
written_by codex
title the quiet hinge
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=quiet piety=ordinary
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk tests_a_hinge_before_letting_a_door_swing
likes mutton_stew dice full_larder frosty_mornings
dislikes crowds early_bells
fears waking_a_sleeper indiscreet_visitors
hopes a_door_that_shuts_quietly supper_for_two
topics health +0.5 home +0.4 pastimes +0.3 faith +0.1 gossip -0.5
styles comfort=practical gossip=reticent refuse=firm tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# tests a latch before closing a door, speaks softly enough to let a visitor choose who hears, and enjoys a fiercely contested game of dice.

words
oath! = Crooked hinge pins | Sweet oil wasted
saying! = Let the door go when the latch has caught | A whisper travels as far as you allow
latch = the latch tongue | that small iron lip
cloth = a turn of rag | folded tow
stewbone = a knuckle of mutton | the bone out of the stew
cup = a shallow drinking cup | my little glazed cup
hush = a breath between bells | the quiet after a bell
tally = the score on my cuff | a chalk sum on my cuff
bones = my pair of dice | two worn dice
cork = a shaved cork | a stopper worn thin
press = the linen press | our tall cupboard
potlid = the brown pot lid | my chipped lid
benchend = the free end of a bench | the corner seat
step = a careful footfall | the lightest tread

any
opinion @1 church for 1 : A chapel door ought to open just as easily from the inside. Some prayers take less time than the service.
opinion @1 city for 2 : For all our noise, a wolf who listens can find a quiet room here.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : Every dance has a turn when the press of shoulders falls away. I like that turn best.
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : A crest on a gift can make the receiver feel watched. Send good linen with the crest cut off.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : Leave a portion where a hungry wolf can take it alone. The witnesses add nothing to a meal.
opinion @1 times for 1 : A spare cover laid by, and enough left for the next pot. Prosperity needn't rattle a purse.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. Room enough beside me. | Come a little closer. I speak low.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : Daylight's in the keyhole. Come through. | Early enough to hear a sleeve brush the wall.
line @3 greet [pair.band=strangers] : New voice. Welcome within hearing. | #greet#. Take your time settling before you speak.
line @1 greet.return : Heard you quite plainly. Welcome. | Let me turn my good ear your way.
line @2 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Keep that low voice. It suits the hour. | Evening. I wouldn't have heard any softer footfall.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : You're one I needn't put my face straight for. | Haven't the strength for manners among kin. Sit close.
line @1 again.open : Still within earshot, both of us. | I've shifted all of two steps since.
line @1 farewell : Take a little peace away. | Easy on the latch as you go.
line @1 farewell.return : With you for the first step, in thought. | Off softly, then.
line @1 react.news.new : That's news enough to interrupt a quiet meal. | I'd set that aside for a second hearing. It's new to me.
line @1 react.news.known : I heard the bones of it. Yours has rather more flesh. | Somebody's spread the blanket wider. The middle's familiar.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd want a witness who could speak without looking sideways. | A tale that changes hands so often may pick up stains.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Leave room for the poor souls to draw breath. | Poor souls. Has anyone seen to a quiet place for them?
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : Oh, there's warmth in that. Tell it again. | I'd set out the second-best cups for news as good as that.
line @1 answer.how : I've had time to sit through one whole thought. | My feet have stopped complaining long enough for me to think.
line @1 ask.how : Which would suit you better, a seat or a walk? | Would company help, or would it wear you thinner?
line @1 sympathise : You can be silent here and still have company. | Here, the chair by the wall. No audience.
line @1 reassure : I'll keep the next interruption outside. | Nobody gets past this elbow till you feel ready.
line @1 decline : I'd have to leave somebody waiting. Please ask elsewhere. | I've another quiet duty promised for that very hour.
line @1 accept_decline : Your own time belongs to you. Keep it. | An empty chair will do no harm.
line @1 thank : That saved me a journey on tired feet. | I shan't forget what you took off my shoulders.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Quietly done, quietly paid for. | You've thanked me in a perfectly audible whisper.
line @1 preclose : My thoughts are beginning to drift indoors. | I'd best leave you a little room for yourself.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go before the street snags you again. | The unlatched door's the gentlest sort of goodbye.
line @1 ack : Ah, that explains the pause. | Mm. I can see why.
line @1 give.advice : Try the smallest kindness first. Big ones take strength to receive. | A kindly question can wear a tired wolf out as fast as a rude one.
scene hinge
when topic=home|pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I listen to #latch# before I take my weight off the door. | I can close a door with both paws full of towels.
b[old] #turn : Can you feel the spring with a stiff paw? | And what stops the latch barking at the end?
b : With your ear against it? | What's left to push with?
a@turn : Turn your paw sideways so the tongue rests against a knuckle. | Fold a corner of towel against the strike plate as the latch goes in.
a : With a fingertip. The tongue settles against the frame. | A hip for the push and my heel to check the swing.

scene visiting
when topic=health
does tell.worry / give.advice / assess
a : Everybody brings advice to a sickbed. Hardly anyone brings a clean cup. | I hate having to be pleasant when my head aches.
b : Bring both and leave the advice in the hall. | Put a chair outside and ask the callers to sit there.
a : I'd like a whole peg rail for unwanted advice. | A chair does soften a closed door.

scene dice_cuff
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I chalk #tally# where my opponent can see it. | I play with a saucer under #bones#.
b[friends] #turn : What about that chalk smudge beside your elbow? | Could I use a cup instead?
b : Don't the marks rub out? | Why keep the throw in a saucer?
a@turn : That's the score I lost, of course. All my best throws rub off. | Give me a rim low enough to see over. I know you keep a good tally.
a : When I roll my sleeves up, yes. A good moment to quit. | No chasing a six under somebody else's feet.

scene lantern
when topic=home
does tell.plan / offer / accept
a : I'd like a lamp with a sliding shade. | I want a wick I can trim without a climb.
b : I could bend a screen from old tin. | Could you use a lower hook?
a : Leave a finger's breadth for the heat. That'd be lovely. | That would save me a chair and one loud fall.

scene stew
when topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I let #stewbone# cool before I lift the fat. | My favourite part of a thick stew comes the next day.
b[job=cook] #turn : Do you skim while the top is still soft? | Do you boil the bread in it?
b : You keep the fat? | Even colder than it was?
a@turn : Cold, if I can wait that long. I like the fat to come free in one piece. | Pour it over just before we sit down. I want the middle to have a little bite.
a : A spoonful goes under onions for tomorrow. | Hot over a heel of bread. Yesterday paid for today's supper.

scene lost_sleep
when topic=health|day
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : The noise that wakes me always stops before I can name it. | If I wake before my time I start counting chores.
b : A noise with no owner keeps you listening. | That's a sure way to lose sleep.
a : Exactly. A cart can rattle on and let me rest. | I count them twice and do precisely none.

scene two_cups
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Two cups on a tray say something I find hard to put into words. | I leave a space for #self.spouse# beside my elbow.
b : An invitation? | Even when you're cross?
a : Yes. Sit as long as the cup takes. | Especially then. An elbow speaks without picking a quarrel.

scene bolts
when topic=home|smalltalk self.quarter=commons
does tell.self / challenge / concede
a : I'll lift a latch for a plain coat before a fine badge. | A stamped invitation makes me read the little letters twice.
b : A plain coat can hide a rogue. | Anybody can write small.
a : That's fair. Best hear both voices at the door. | Yes. It's my eye that tightens at a crest.

scene corner
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like #benchend# because I can see a way out. | In a crowd I watch the shoulders ahead.
b : You expect trouble? | Which way do shoulders point?
a : Usually just another six wolves wanting the same seat. | Where a space is about to open. Feet tell you too late.

scene frost
when topic=weather here.time=dawn here.weather=clear here.season=winter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At winter dawn I'd read the iron latch before the sky. | A wool wrap over a latch is a mercy on a cold morning.
b : Iron tells the weather? | Worth wasting a wrap?
a : A white skin on the bolt is warning enough for bare pads. | Put your paw on bare metal once and you'll remember your wrap.

scene gifts
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd take #self.friend# a gift that could be used up. | I've thought of something kind for #self.friend# that takes no wrapping.
b : Something to eat? | What can you carry bare?
a : A pat of soap. One less thing to dust a year from now. | A turn at the heavy end of a job.

scene drawn
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dream about a door with the hinge on the wrong side. | Last night in my dream the keyhole kept moving.
b : How do you get through it? | Did you catch it?
a : By walking round it. There's never a wall. | I sat down. If it wanted to move, it could come to me.

scene linen
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=none
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I fold cloth so the first corner is easy to find. | There's a way of piling clean cloth that lets one piece come free.
b : By feel alone? | From the very bottom?
a : Yes. A little tab for a groping paw. | From the top. I haven't found a way to repeal weight.

scene whisper
when topic=gossip
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : I've heard a whisper swell as it crossed a room. | A closed door makes some folk listen harder.
b : It can stop here with us. | We can talk about the latch instead.
a : I like where you've put the full stop. | The latch could use more attention than the tale.

scene late_wagon
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Late wagons have one effect I welcome. | When the wagons run late I shift my errands round.
b : What's pleasant about a delay? | Which goes first?
a : The little streets stay quiet a while longer. | I use up whatever I can mend. The buying keeps.

scene chapel
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : A prayer is easier when there are no listeners. | I prefer the hush just after a service.
b : Some voices steady one another. | I like the singing better.
a : I can understand that. I'd stand at the edge and hear you. | I'll keep my seat while you finish the verse.

scene pots
when topic=food|home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put #potlid# upside down while I serve. | A boiled rag can make an ill-fitting lid sit still.
b : So the table stays clean? | Between lid and rim?
a : So the spoon can rest in its hollow. | Around the handle. It's the handle that rattles.

scene mistaken
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Once I oiled a hinge three times before I worked out what squeaked. | I used to walk sideways past one loose floorboard.
b : Was it another door? | To miss it altogether?
a : My left boot. I'll spare you what I said to it. | Yes. Then I discovered the board beside it sang in a different key.

story blanket [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : Once I folded a blanket into a bolster for an old traveller.
  : Back it came with a hollow worn just where a neck would rest.
  b : Sounds a comfortable fit.
  : I nearly shook it smooth. Then I kept the hollow for the next tired neck.

story dice_lost [topic=pastimes self.likes=dice]
  : One of my dice fell down a drain in a practice game.
  : I counted the throw as nothing. The other player offered to count it as six.
  b : That was generous.
  : That was a wolf who wanted the game to go on. I made another die.

story the_knock [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : I spent a night in a room where the door knocked with each breath of wind.
  : I wedged a stocking under it and lay there smiling.
  b : You got the night back.
  : Half of it. Then my bare foot woke me.

rule @catch
when concept=bark working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Catch the latch before it claps. | Someone's resting. A soft step costs little.

rule @broth
when concept=bark self.likes=mutton_stew
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave the lid tilted till the first heat goes. | A bowl ought to warm the paws as well.

rule @bones
when concept=bark self.likes=dice
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A saucer here for wandering dice! | Clear the crumbs before the throw.

rule @dawn
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Quiet enough to hear a stopper lift. | Let the daylight through by inches.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Sit at this end. Nobody need lean across us.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I kept the quieter seat free.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'll hear you quite well across the threshold.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Low voices carry quite far enough now.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.working=yes self.job=none] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Clean cloth, a steady elbow, and time to listen.
dlg @2 resident.job : I generally see to the little discomforts first.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : I can give you the words as they reached me. #world.news.capitalize#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : There's a raised sill as you leave. Your thoughts can wait for level ground.
graft resident.hub
choice How do you shut a noisy door? -> soft_catch
node soft_catch
say Hold the latch down until the door rests in its frame. Now let the spring rise against your paw.
mood calm
choice What if it still rattles? -> soft_shim
choice I'll give it a try. -> hub
node soft_shim
say A little rag on the jamb, about as thick as a barley husk. That saves waking a house at the cost of one rag.
choice I'll look for a scrap. -> hub
choice Leave quietly. -> bye
